## Building index: 
module load kallisto/0.48.0
cd ~/knowles_lab/index/kallisto/mus_musculus/with_precursor
kb ref -i index.idx -g t2g.txt -f1 cdna.fa -f2 intron.fa -c1 cdna_t2c.txt -c2 intron_t2c.txt --workflow lamanno GRCm39.primary_assembly.genome.fa.gz gencode.vM32.basic.annotation.gtf.gz
This gives a "transcript" for every intron separately, which I don't think is what I want. 
Instead try to use gffread: 
module load stringtie/2.1.6
see e.g. https://www.biostars.org/p/386742/
http://ccb.jhu.edu/software/stringtie/gff.shtml

module load htslib/1.17
module load samtools/1.17
samtools faidx GRCm39.primary_assembly.genome.fa

gffread -F -w transcripts.fa -s seq_info.txt -g GRCm39.primary_assembly.genome.fa <( zcat gencode.vM32.basic.annotation.gtf.gz )

module load bedtools/2.29.0

module load bedops/2.4.35

bedtools getfasta -name -s -fi GRCm39.primary_assembly.genome.fa -bed genes.gtf -fo precursors.fa

## Barcode matches

The 96 length 8 BCs for the three stages (RT and two ligation steps) seem to be the same. 
This makes distinguishing which is which more tricky. In the sequence, the first and second 8bp parts of the BC match the whitelist pretty well. The third however range(16:24) does not, even if I reverse or reverse complement the sequence. This is the part of the BC which should be used to match the polyDT and random hexamers from the first round :(